-- Baseline: the schema that migrations 0000-0015 produced, as one file.
--
-- Generated by applying the old chain to an empty database and running
-- pg_dump --schema-only --no-owner --no-privileges -n public. The old chain
-- also carried store rows, a product harvest and fixes to both; none of that
-- is here. A fresh database gets its rows from the private collector's seed
-- or from a restored dump.
--
-- Its journal `when` equals the old 0015's, so a database that already ran
-- the old chain (production) treats this as applied and skips it. The
-- migrator compares timestamps only, never file contents.
--
-- pg_trgm is guarded as in the old 0002: without the extension, product
-- search still works, it just scans.
DO $$
BEGIN
  CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pg_trgm;
EXCEPTION WHEN insufficient_privilege THEN
  RAISE NOTICE 'pg_trgm not installed: product search falls back to a sequential scan';
END $$;
